New finite-kernel generator, certificate checker, proof and package metadata:
ToikY, with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. Apache-2.0.

The two source files are retained verbatim from Nick Petalas's PR6425, exact
head092dcbd13d1263e691ad29f34fbf286fea1fac2c. Their original headings and credit
remain. SOURCE-PINS.json records exact Git blob identities, byte lengths and
SHA256 digests; no predecessor executable is imported or replayed.

Retain predecessor credit to Jeremy Diviney/PR1422 for the complete-clique guard,
geometry/caps and smaller-family question; Cinna Davis/PR1347/1323 for the support
model and geometry; Navinor, David Arias, Hanson Sun, DreamingOfClouds,
themilkman216 and the retained E8/label/decoder lineage.

PR5767 is related exact-certificate tooling, not the source of an optimization
solver here. Its shared limits and code are unchanged. Linear programming,
nonnegative implication/Farkas certificates, simplex and Bland's rule are
classical methods; no literature priority is claimed.
